{
  "item": "Worm01",
  "mu_name": "Worm",
  "mu_name_from": "MuMain's _enum.h: MONSTER_MODEL_WORM = 17, so OpenMonsterModel loads Monster{17 + 1}, Monster18.bmd. The client's name is 웜, the English word in Hangul; OpenMU's Version075 Devias.cs:227-245 names number 24 'Worm' at level 20 with 600 health, 75-80 damage, 25 defense, MoveRange 3, AttackRange 1, ViewRange 4, AttackDelay 1600, respawn 10 s. Sixty-five of them in 128-251 by 0-128, the town's quarter of the map (Devias.cs:68).\n\nIt is not a worm. The rig is a biped -- two thighs, calves, feet and toes -- with a long spine, a head and a three-bone jaw chain (Bone01-03 under Bip01 Head) and a tail box on the pelvis.",
  "world": "devias",
  "object_type": 24,
  "monster": {
    "model_index": 17,
    "scale": 1.0
  },
  "monster_from": "ZzzCharacter.cpp:14008-14012, CreateMonster, case MONSTER_WORM:\n\n    OpenMonsterModel(MONSTER_MODEL_WORM);\n    c = CreateCharacter(Key, MODEL_WORM, PositionX, PositionY);\n    wcscpy(c->ID, L\"웜\");\n\nNothing else: no weapon, no Scale (so 1.0), no BlendMesh, no Level. Its only other line in the client is the bounding box it shares with the Budge Dragon, the Spider and the Goblin (ZzzCharacter.cpp:11806-11812, 50 by 50 by 80).",
  "profile": "monster",
  "rig_from": "Seven actions, slots 0 to 6, exported with --actions=0,1,2,3,4,5,6. Keys: 12, 12, 7, 9, 9, 13, 11. 24 bones, four of them dummies.\n\nPlay speeds are OpenMonsterModel's defaults with one override: `case MONSTER_MODEL_WORM: b->Actions[MONSTER01_WALK].PlaySpeed = 0.5f;` (ZzzOpenData.cpp:2626), against the table's 0.34 -- twelve and a half keys a second over a seven-key stride, a scurry. 17 is not in the multiplier list. No BoneHead is set in its sound case, so the model keeps the default.",
  "sheets": {
    "garp": "worm_garp.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "One sheet, Data/Monster/garp.OZJ, 64 by 64, no alpha; the .bmd's one mesh reads garp.jpg (258 triangles). Decoded under a worm_ prefix so the file says whose it is.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "garp": "fur"
  },
  "sheet_materials_from": "Read off the sheet at 8x: a grey-brown shaggy hide in long streaks, white along the ridge of the back and the tail, over a red open maw with a row of white fangs. The hide is most of it and it is hair, not scale -- fur, as the Agon's. The mouth is a small corner of the one island and takes the fur's values; it is dark red painted, and the paint carries it.",
  "effects_from": "None. MODEL_WORM appears in ZzzCharacter.cpp in CreateMonster and in the bounding-box switch alone -- not in MoveCharacterVisual's per-frame switch, not in RenderCharacter's, and not in the missile code. It raises nothing while it walks, fights or dies, and it bites: AttackRange 1 and no AttackSkill in OpenMU.",
  "sounds_from": "ZzzOpenData.cpp:3489-3494: mWorm1, mWorm2 and mWormDie loaded, then SetMonsterSound(..., 53, 53, 55, 55, 55). Offsets from SOUND_MONSTER_BULL1: 53 is WORM1 and 55 is WORMDIE, so it moves to mWorm1 alone, and it swings, flinches and dies to mWormDie -- mWorm2 is loaded and never played. Wired as worm_* in sounds.json.",
  "islands_from": "24 islands for 258 triangles -- the mirrored halves split, and the jaw, tail and toes in small runs. All fur: they arrived as skin, the monster profile's default (the trap Spider01 records), and were set by hand to the sheet's reading.",
